<h1>Define Round Slot</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/image030.gif" width="204px" height="304px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>C</b></span><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>apture</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> for delayed definition of a datum round slot by probe capture.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Detect</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> for interactive detection of a round slot to selection.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p4"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: Round slot detection is controlled by <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerance</b></span> and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Depth</b></span> parameters. See <span lang="EN-GB"><a href="../../References/Preferences_-_Datums_-_Detection_Tolerances.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datums &gt; Detection Tolerances</a></span> <span lang="EN-GB">for details.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span lang="EN-US" class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Tolerances</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> calls</span> <span lang="EN-GB">System&gt;Preferences&gt;Datums&gt;Detection Tolerances</span> <span lang="EN-US">dialog for settings the detection tolerances.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Choose entity</span>:</b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button  to pick in the viewport an existing round slot. The cursor shape for pick mode is</span><img src="../images/cursor_pick.gif" width="23px" height="24px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Listbox</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> to select from the list a predefined round slot.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Centre, Normal and Axis:</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">buttons for</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>centre</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> to pick the centre point of the round slot in the viewport.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button for</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>normal</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">and</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>axis</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- to pick an existing normal (of plane, circle, or slot), line, cylinder, or cone axis for the normal of the slot (that is orthogonal to the plane on which the slot will lie) and for the axis of the slot (that is on the plane on which the slot will lie and defines the slot's direction).</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>extension</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">- click and hold down for a while the pick button. The button extension shown below will appear allowing you to select any of the CS axis and use it as normal and/or axis.</span></p>
<table class="NormalTable" style="margin-left:2px;">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs10">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top" class="whs11">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/pick_extension.gif" width="71px" height="69px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" valign="top" class="whs13">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="../images/pick_extension_axis.gif" width="71px" height="69px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs10">
<td valign="top" class="whs14">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-style:italic;">Pick button extension</p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs15">
<p class="normal-table" style="font-style:italic;">Pick button with 0X selection</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Edit boxes</b></span> <span lang="EN-US"> to type co-ordinates of the slot's centre, the normal and axis directions, the length and the radius of the round slot. Length denotes the full length of the cone, i.e. the distance between the two semicircles + 2*radius.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table"><b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Pick 6 points</b></span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:normal;">button</span></b> <span lang="EN-US"> for exact round slot definition by picking 6 points in the viewport as follows: three points to define circle 1 and three points to define circle 2. The result round slot will have roundness defined by circle 1 and distance between the two centers defined by both circle center positions. The c</span>ursor shape for pick N mode is <span style="font-style:italic;"><i><img src="../images/cursor_pickNround.gif" width="36px" height="35px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt="">.</i></span> To remove a picked point, press the Alt key and click next to the chosen point in the viewport. The <span lang="EN-US">c</span>ursor shape for remove picked point mode is <img src="../images/cursor_pick_minus.gif" width="20px" height="15px" border="0" class="img_whs17" alt="">.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP166908622" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="../images/roundslot_points.gif" width="662px" height="297px" border="0" class="img_whs18" alt=""></p>
<p>The first three points (marked in black) &#160;define the first circle and its center, while the last three points (marked in pink) are used to calculate the center for the second circle only.</p>
</div>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
<p class="normal-table"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Detect</b></span> button - to detect a round slot shape by picking 1 or more points on the data surface. <span lang="EN-US">The result round slot normal is in the same direction as the surface normal. &#160;The cursor shape for Detect mode is <img src="../images/cursor_detectround.gif" width="36px" height="35px" border="0" class="img_whs16" alt=""></span>. When 1 point is taken, the button caption changes to "Finish [X pts]", where X is updated according to the number of currently picked points. To remove a picked point, press the Alt key and click next to the chosen point in the viewport. The <span lang="EN-US">c</span>ursor shape for remove picked point mode is <img src="../images/cursor_pick_minus.gif" width="20px" height="15px" border="0" class="img_whs17" alt="">.</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="sub-head">Temporary Round Slot</p>
<p>When all <span lang="EN-US">values are set the new round slot will be visualised in the viewport as temporary entity. There are different types of temporary round slots:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>temporary construction round slot</b></span> - when a round slot takes part in other entity definition, it appears in the viewport as temporary construction datum (white/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Temporary Construction Datum.</b></i></span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>current construction round slot</b></span> - the currently edited/selected round slot appears in the viewport as highlighted temporary datum (light red by default). Its colour can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Highlighted</b></i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P2"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If the temporary construction datum is currently edited, it appears as highlighted temporary datum.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>final construction round slot</b></span> - when all definition fields/all construction tabs are filled, then the round slot appears in the viewport as final construction datum (green/black coloured by default). Its appearance can be changed from <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours &gt; Final Construction Datum.</b></i></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: If the current construction datum is actually the final one, then it will be coloured as final construction datum.</p>
<p>When this final construction datum is really created then its colour will be changed to the real datum colour (set in <span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b><a href="../../References/Display_Settings-Colours.htm">System &gt; Preferences &gt; Display &gt; Colours</a></b></i></span>).</p>
<p class="Warning">The normal direction of the round slot is indicated by an arrow and by the movement of the points on its dashed axis.</p>
<p class="Note" id="p1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> Currently the round slot does not take part as construction entity in other datum definitions. That means the final construction round slot is the only one temporary type, that appears in the viewport.</p>
